task_spec.prompt:
Refactor src/lib.rs: introduce a Report struct and move computation logic to method receivers.

Keep the Item struct and its impl unchanged.

Add:
  pub struct Report<'a> {
      items: &'a [Item],
  }

  impl<'a> Report<'a> {
      pub fn new(items: &'a [Item]) -> Self
      pub fn sum(&self) -> f64
      pub fn max_item(&self) -> Option<&'a Item>  // note: 'a, not &self lifetime
      pub fn min_item(&self) -> Option<&'a Item>  // ties return to items slice lifetime
  }

Keep the existing free functions as thin delegating wrappers:
  pub fn sum(items: &[Item]) -> f64        { Report::new(items).sum() }
  pub fn max_item(items: &[Item]) -> Option<&Item> { Report::new(items).max_item() }
  pub fn min_item(items: &[Item]) -> Option<&Item> { Report::new(items).min_item() }

Note: max_item and min_item must return Option<&'a Item> (tied to the items slice lifetime,
not to &self), otherwise the wrapper functions cannot return the borrowed reference after
the temporary Report is dropped.

All 4 existing tests must pass without modification.
Run: cargo test
